# jewelry-girvi-app

## Non-negotiable: verify APIs before writing code
This project runs Expo SDK 57, React Native 0.86.2, React 19.2.3,
TypeScript 6.0.3. These are newer than your training data. Before using
ANY Expo or React Native API, fetch the versioned doc page at
https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v57.0.0/ and cite the URL you read.
If you cannot fetch it, say so and stop. Do not write from memory.

## Stack — as installed, not as imagined
- Router: expo-router 57, typedRoutes enabled
- UI: @expo/ui (native primitives) + expo-glass-effect. 
  DO NOT install react-native-paper, nativewind, tailwind, or any other
  UI framework. If you believe one is needed, ask first.
- Backend: @supabase/supabase-js 2.112.3
- Session storage: expo-secure-store
- React Compiler is ON — do not hand-write useMemo/useCallback unless
  profiling justifies it.

## Security rules (these are the ones that matter)
- Data isolation is enforced by Postgres RLS using auth.uid(), never by
  client-side .eq() filters. A client filter is UX, not a boundary.
- Admin (shop owner) vs customer (borrower) privilege is decided
  server-side in an RLS policy. Never by a boolean in client state.
- Every new table ships with its migration file AND its RLS policies in
  the same change. A table without RLS is not done.
- Storage buckets are private. Access via signed URLs only. Object paths
  are namespaced by user id.
- service_role key never appears in app code.

## TypeScript
- strict is on. No `any` on Supabase responses. No @ts-ignore.
- DB types must be generated, not hand-written.

## Platform
- iOS and Android both ship. @expo/ui and expo-glass-effect components
  need an explicit Android fallback path — state it when you use one.